e root $x=2$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=2$ is a simple root, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the roots $x=0,1$ is $2,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at these points.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{I}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is negative, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $-\\infty .$\n\nOnly graph $\\text{IV}$ displays this end behavior. Therefore, the correct answer is $\\text{IV}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dc60b75-554d-58d0-b027-ef3b794160a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{III}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245720} {:answer/id #uuid "c7100d83-8d57-52e6-94e1-b855e81e9f6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246077} {:answer/id #uuid "ce812ba4-0a43-5778-955c-7bd1edb83e74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246159} {:answer/id #uuid "dbae5fd7-431f-5c98-a632-966ebf920961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246265} {:answer/id #uuid "e210e43b-42d1-5c93-91f6-fb894fd6ce1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7100d83-8d57-52e6-94e1-b855e81e9f6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246077} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2ce298d-c1f9-5147-8aa9-67f9aa805a1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246873}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.d